1
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:12,440
If doing this makes you feel better,

2
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,720
then keep doing it.

3
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,400
But believe me.

4
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:17,440
‎PREVIOUSLY

5
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,520
It won't actually make you feel better.

6
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:21,360
What is it now?

7
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:24,440
It's Ramil. He's slacking off.
He refuses to come to work.

8
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:27,720
Aunt Liu brought Pong in
to supervise the work instead of you.

9
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:31,520
You're always criticizing
everyone else for being selfish,

10
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,560
but you never look at yourself.

11
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:35,720
You're being just as selfish as they are.

12
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,840
I've never been selfish.

13
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,840
Then what do you call this?

14
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:49,640
Why did you want me to supervise
the work instead of Ramil?

15
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:53,160
Ramil controls everything,

16
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,800
even the purchasing prices.

17
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,840
That means I can’t adjust
any of the figures.

18
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,360
Don’t worry, Ms. Liu.

19
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:06,920
Now that I’m supervising the work,

20
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:09,840
whatever you want,
however you want it done,

21
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,760
I can make it happen.

22
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:18,920
Go supervise the work.
Pressure those workers until they quit.

23
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:22,160
Then bring in new workers.

24
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:24,080
Find people with some actual skills.

25
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:28,920
I’ll even let you take a cut
from the workers’ wages.

26
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,120
With that kind of freedom,

27
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:36,880
I couldn’t be happier.

28
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:40,600
Whatever you want,

29
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,040
however you want it,

30
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:44,200
just tell me.

31
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:55,520
Miss Hathaya, help!
I can’t handle this anymore.

32
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,240
Where’s your boss?

33
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:59,880
He still hasn’t come to work.
Please help me.

34
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,280
What happened?

35
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:02,880
Come on.

36
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:11,400
Don’t you understand plain language?
I told you to go work over there.

37
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,680
But this part still isn’t finished, boss.

38
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:15,440
Can I finish this first?

39
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:18,440
Ramil told us that whatever we do,
we should do it properly

40
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:19,520
and treat it like our home.

41
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:22,320
-You talking back to me?!
-You okay?

42
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:25,680
I’m your boss now. You listen to me!

43
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:28,840
Why couldn't you just talk to him?
Why hit him?

44
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:30,320
Stay out of it!

45
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:31,800
Ya.

46
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:35,440
What? What are you going to do about it?

47
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,760
Ya, are you all right?

48
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,120
Yes.

49
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:44,680
Don’t you understand human language?
You damn aliens.

50
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,520
We’re human too.

51
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:48,280
Show us some respect.

52
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:50,760
Why the hell should I respect you?

53
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:53,160
I’m your boss now.

54
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:56,120
Every one of you has to listen to me.

55
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:59,320
Boss Ramil never treated us like this.

56
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,720
He respected us.

57
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,760
-That’s right.
-That’s right.

58
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:03,920
That’s right.

59
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,160
Ramil never oppressed or mistreated us.

60
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,280
Stop talking about him!

61
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,080
I’m your supervisor now.

62
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:14,080
Every one of you here has to listen to me.

63
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,600
You’ve gone too far.

64
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:18,880
They came here to work.
They’re not prisoners.

65
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:21,360
Miss Hathaya, I’m sorry

66
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,680
if I’ve upset you,

67
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:25,160
but what I’m doing

68
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,200
is teaching these workers

69
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,920
how things are done here.

70
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:32,520
Otherwise, they’ll never learn to obey.

71
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,800
Show them some respect
when you speak to them.

72
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,320
Hathaya,

73
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:41,080
you’re lecturing other people
about respect?

74
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:44,480
Then show Pong some respect too.

75
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,720
He’s the foreman.

76
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:49,840
It’s his job to manage the workers.
This has nothing to do with you.

77
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,160
Go back to your own work.

78
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:53,760
I never interfere
in other people’s business

79
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:55,840
unless it affects Grandpa’s work.

80
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:58,200
I don’t see how anything
is being affected.

81
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:00,520
The foreman you brought in

82
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,600
is abusing his authority
and mistreating the workers.

83
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:05,400
If they can’t take it and all quit,

84
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,160
Grandpa’s development will come to a halt.

85
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:09,160
Reserved houses could get canceled

86
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,720
if they aren't done in time.

87
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:14,840
You haven’t even been
working here for a full month.

88
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,440
Don’t act like you know everything.

89
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:18,960
I’ve helped Father with this for years.

90
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:21,320
I’m not going to let
the development suffer.

91
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:24,920
If these workers want to quit, let them.

92
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,920
There’s no reason
to beg them to stay. Parasites.

93
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,320
Pong

94
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,680
has worked on major construction projects.

95
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,680
He has plenty of contacts and workers,

96
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:39,200
and they’re much more skilled.
Unlike these people.

97
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:40,840
They have no real skills.

98
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:44,120
They’re low-level laborers
with no quality.

99
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:48,080
If Father hadn’t given them
a chance to work here,

100
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:51,920
they’d probably be begging
on the street by now.

101
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,160
Madam, if you think we have no value

102
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:58,240
and no skills, then I quit.

103
00:07:58,760 --> 00:07:59,760
I quit too.

104
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:00,760
Me too.

105
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:02,480
-Me too.
-Me too.

106
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:05,960
-Let's all quit.
-Hey! Quiet!

107
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:10,120
I never told any of you to leave,

108
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:12,840
but if you want to quit,

109
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,840
I’m not going to stop you.

110
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:17,920
Pack your things and get out
of my development.

111
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:20,880
Let’s go.

112
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,040
-Come on.
-Let's go.

113
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:24,200
-Let's go.
-Go.

114
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:25,800
Wait. Please don’t leave yet.

115
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:29,880
Calm down. I’ll talk to Mr. Pichai

116
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:32,960
and ask him to resolve this.
Please calm down first.

117
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:36,240
Hathaya, we really can’t take it anymore.

118
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:38,960
You can work us as hard
as you want, and we can endure that.

119
00:08:39,039 --> 00:08:41,480
But being spoken to
like we’re not even human?

120
00:08:41,559 --> 00:08:43,320
We can’t accept that.

121
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,560
I’m truly sorry, Hathaya.

122
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:47,720
Aow. Could you please calm down

123
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,600
and wait until Ramil comes back,

124
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:51,680
then make your decision? Please.

125
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,920
Boss has been very good to us.

126
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:56,560
We love him,

127
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:59,240
but he abandoned us.

128
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,520
So we’re leaving too.

129
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:06,240
Then follow your old boss out!
Quit and go after him.

130
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,360
-Let's go.
-Yeah.

131
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,280
Go on! Shoo!

132
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:10,760
Everyone, go back to work.

133
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:12,840
That’s an order.

134
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:28,280
Sir, here are the latest
reservation figures.

135
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:31,320
Alright. Has Liu come in yet?

136
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:32,960
Yes, she has.

137
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,040
Then where is she?

138
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,440
Why did you come back?

139
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:40,600
If you want to take time off,
then stay away as long as you want.

140
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:41,960
Or just quit.

141
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:46,440
Well? Why are you still here? Go!

142
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:47,880
Nobody is going anywhere.

143
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,120
How is this your business?

144
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,720
They’re my workers.

145
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:53,280
Touch my people,

146
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,120
and you deal with me.

147
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,160
Stop it.

148
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:58,800
Pong works for me.

149
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,480
He’s the new foreman.

150
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,680
You have no right to interfere.

151
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:04,680
Mr. Pichai hasn’t fired me.

152
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,160
I’m still responsible for these people.

153
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:10,560
But I’m his daughter-in-law.
I outrank you.

154
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:15,440
Yes. You’re the project owner’s
daughter-in-law.

155
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,640
You do outrank me.

156
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:20,360
But these people are mine.

157
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,360
You dare argue with me?

158
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:25,200
Fine. I’ll tell Father

159
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,880
to fire you along with all of them.

160
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:31,160
Aunt Liu, you don’t need to tell him.

161
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:38,600
Father, Ramil is causing chaos here.

162
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:42,160
Don’t say another word.
Come talk to me in the office.

163
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:44,520
Yes, Father.

164
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:45,680
Ramil.

165
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:49,480
-We need to talk.
-Yes, sir.

166
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,600
He's probably angry
because Ramil missed work.

167
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,960
If Ms. Liu keeps stirring things up,
he's definitely in trouble.

168
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:08,960
Grandpa is reasonable.
He won’t listen to only one side.

169
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,080
That’s absolutely right.

170
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:14,680
He won’t listen to one side.
He’ll listen to both sides.

171
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:17,840
One side is Madam. The other side is Pong.

172
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:19,240
As for Ramil?

173
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:21,560
He’s all alone.

174
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,480
He’s finished.

175
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:32,960
No one is working. What happened?

176
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:34,720
It’s Ramil.

177
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,400
He missed work and caused problems.

178
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:39,520
And he even stirred up the workers
to turn against Pong.

179
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:43,000
I tried my very best to take care
of my workers, sir.

180
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:45,200
I never abused my authority over them.

181
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:48,120
I never even thought
of myself as their boss.

182
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:51,120
I see all of them as my coworkers.

183
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,120
But I don’t know

184
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:55,680
what Ramil told them.

185
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,360
They refuse to listen to me.

186
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,480
That makes my job very difficult, sir.

187
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:04,880
I have never taught
my people to defy anyone.

188
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:08,600
And I have no reason to do that.

189
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:13,280
If the workers refuse to respect you,

190
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:16,240
maybe you should take a look at yourself

191
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:19,520
and ask why you can’t manage them.

192
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:22,640
The problem isn’t Pong.

193
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:25,840
It’s your workers.
They’re not skilled enough.

194
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:27,520
They work slowly.

195
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:30,080
And many of those villagers you brought in

196
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:33,760
have no experience. You teach them,
but it goes in one ear and out the other.

197
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:36,040
I admit

198
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:38,920
the new workers may not
be highly skilled yet,

199
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,120
but they learn quickly, they’re generous,

200
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:44,200
and they'll work hard
to finish the job on schedule.

201
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:46,720
This is a business. It’s not a charity

202
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,640
or a training center.

203
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:52,960
Father, Pong has a professional team

204
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:55,360
ready to come in immediately.

205
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:58,080
I say we get rid of the old workers

206
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:01,560
and replace them with Pong’s team.

207
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:07,480
Don’t take too long deciding, Father.

208
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:10,560
Not before more damage is done.

209
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:18,200
Pong.

210
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,440
Bring your people in to work here.

211
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:27,280
Thank you, sir.

212
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:31,280
Ramil.

213
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:35,000
You know you were wrong
to abandon your work, don’t you?

214
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,960
Yes. I accept responsibility.

215
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:40,120
Good. If you know you did wrong,

216
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:42,680
then you must accept the consequences.

217
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,120
Yes, sir.

218
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:57,640
They still haven’t come out, Max.

219
00:13:58,320 --> 00:13:59,320
Well,

220
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:02,880
something like this takes time.

221
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:05,560
Mr. Pichai is firing Ramil.

222
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:08,200
Ramil is probably

223
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:10,240
crying,

224
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:13,200
clinging to his legs,
and begging for mercy.

225
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:16,360
-Serves him right.
-Serves who right?

226
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,960
Serves me right.

227
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:20,520
You should all go back to work.

228
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,640
We’ve made our decision.

229
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:25,760
If Ramil gets fired, we’re leaving too.

230
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:30,760
He's coming.

231
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:43,640
Madam! What did Mr. Pichai say?

232
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:46,680
Pong,

233
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:48,760
Father ordered you to bring in your team.

234
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:50,160
Call your people.

235
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,680
Heaven has eyes!

236
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:56,400
Master wants premium quality,

237
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,920
not defective goods like these people.

238
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,160
If you leave, I’m leaving too.

239
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,160
Yes.

240
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:06,040
I and the others will go with Boss.

241
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,200
Yes.

242
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:12,800
What are all of you doing?

243
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,000
Why aren’t you back at work yet?

244
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:24,040
Mr. Pichai reprimanded me
for failing to submit a leave request,

245
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:27,800
and he ordered me to continue
taking care of all of you.

246
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:30,640
Good!

247
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,040
Very good.

248
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:37,600
Sir, then why are you letting
Pong bring in another team?

249
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:41,120
Phase One is completely sold out.

250
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:43,160
I need to launch Phase Two
as soon as possible.

251
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,680
So Pong

252
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:48,080
is bringing in another team.
We’ll have two teams working.

253
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:51,120
As long as Ramil is still
our supervisor, we’ll keep working.

254
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:55,200
Boss, don’t take any more days off.
We missed you.

255
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:57,200
Don’t leave again, okay?

256
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:59,200
Okay?

257
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:01,080
We missed you so much.

258
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:02,520
Right, everyone?

259
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:04,280
Be with us.

260
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:05,240
Missed you so much.

261
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,160
Yeah.

262
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,080
All right, everyone.

263
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:16,240
Work like you normally do.
No need to be nervous.

264
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:18,680
If you want to sing, sing.
If you want to dance, dance.

265
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:21,320
Just don’t let the work suffer.

266
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:22,520
Go. Go. Go.

267
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:26,120
When Boss is gone, I get a migraine.
Now we can finally breathe again!

268
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:30,800
-Back to work, everyone!
-Come on!

269
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,760
Why did you decide to come back?

270
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:48,440
Who are you asking?

271
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,240
You.

272
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:51,920
If you’re asking me,

273
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,680
turn around and talk to me.

274
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:58,520
Don't just say things. I thought
some wandering ghost was talking to me.

275
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,200
You really do have a nasty mouth.

276
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:05,240
Well? Why did you change your mind?

277
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,720
I want to save money and build a house.

278
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:19,319
I don’t expect anymore that the house

279
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:22,200
has to have both Mom and Dad in it.

280
00:17:25,319 --> 00:17:27,040
I just want to build my own home.

281
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:30,280
My own safe place.

282
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,800
I think that’s a really good idea.

283
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:37,000
If we don’t expect too much,
we won’t be disappointed.

284
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:57,600
Thank you for changing your mind
and coming back to help the workers.

285
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:01,880
If they had all quit,
it would’ve been a disaster.

286
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:05,720
Hey.

287
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,080
When are you gonna start
thinking about yourself?

288
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,200
You always worry about others.

289
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:14,160
I told you already.

290
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,680
If they quit,

291
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:19,320
it affects my sales too.

292
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:22,560
Actually, I’m not doing this
for anyone else.

293
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,600
I’m doing it for myself.

294
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:28,440
I’m going to work here
until the end of the month.

295
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:31,600
Then I can take the money to pay
for my grandma’s treatment.

296
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,440
I want to apologize to you again, sir,

297
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:56,960
for causing all these problems.

298
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:01,000
I know what kind of person you are.
If there hadn’t been a serious problem,

299
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:03,120
this wouldn’t have happened.

300
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:06,160
I…

301
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:10,160
I had some problems with my parents.

302
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:13,280
But that’s no excuse

303
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,120
for making other people suffer too.

304
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:18,000
Remember what I’m about to tell you.

305
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:21,120
No family is perfect.

306
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:24,040
Many of my friends envy me

307
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:26,400
for running a successful business

308
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,480
and think I live happily.

309
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:33,560
But the truth is, it isn’t that happy.

310
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,520
If I could choose,

311
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:40,320
I’d only ask to have enough to live on

312
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:43,440
and to be surrounded by my family,
my kids, grandkids, and loved ones.

313
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:48,800
Sometimes what makes us unhappy

314
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:52,680
is expecting too much from our families.

315
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,600
If we don’t expect too much,

316
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:57,440
we won’t be disappointed.

317
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:01,280
You

318
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:03,680
sound exactly like someone, sir.

319
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:06,960
Who?

320
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:09,320
Hathaya.

321
00:20:10,560 --> 00:20:13,000
You didn’t come all the way to my house

322
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,760
just to apologize, did you?

323
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,400
No, sir.

324
00:20:16,920 --> 00:20:19,040
I wanted to talk to you about Hathaya.

325
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:56,320
I swear on my honor as a man

326
00:20:57,200 --> 00:21:01,120
that nothing happened
between Hathaya and me that night.

327
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:06,200
There was another man
who tried to force himself on her.

328
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:09,880
Hathaya isn’t what everyone thinks she is.

329
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:14,680
Why are you telling me this?

330
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:17,760
Hathaya is your granddaughter.

331
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:21,560
I don’t want her to struggle
because she has to live with me.

332
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,280
If possible,

333
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,800
I’d like you

334
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:29,360
to let her come back and live here.

335
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:34,600
You’ve worked for me a long time.

336
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:37,160
I know what kind of person you are.

337
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:40,040
I believe you.

338
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:45,720
If you believe me, does that mean

339
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:48,840
you’ll let Hathaya come back here?

340
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:54,680
Hathaya is safer
living with you than she is here.

341
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:12,360
Father should’ve fired Ramil already.

342
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:15,320
I’ve hated him for a long time.
I don’t even want to see his face.

343
00:22:15,920 --> 00:22:17,920
I don’t want to see you either, Ms. Liu.

344
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:22,480
Ramil. Why did you come to see Father?

345
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:24,720
It’s personal.

346
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:27,720
Tell me. What did you come
whining to Father about this time?

347
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:30,960
I really don’t think

348
00:22:31,040 --> 00:22:32,720
you understand human language, Ms. Liu.

349
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:34,320
Harsh.

350
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:39,160
I already told you. It’s a private matter
between him and me.

351
00:22:39,240 --> 00:22:42,400
As for you, Ms. Liu, you’re an outsider.

352
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:51,360
See you at the site.

353
00:22:56,920 --> 00:23:00,120
I really want to know
what he talked to Father about.

354
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:13,960
Then who broke into
Hathaya’s room that night?

355
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:18,400
Ms. Sanguansri?

356
00:23:19,520 --> 00:23:20,440
Ms. Sanguansri?

357
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,320
Aunt Sanguansri went out with Dad.

358
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:29,800
Is something wrong?

359
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:33,520
I made a big pot of curry

360
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:35,840
and wanted to bring
some over for all of you.

361
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:42,520
It smells delicious.

362
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:45,840
Thank you.

363
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:50,000
I should get going.

364
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:52,200
Stay and talk for a while.

365
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:55,000
I have work to do.

366
00:23:56,320 --> 00:23:57,200
Hathaya!

367
00:23:57,800 --> 00:24:00,680
Hathaya, wait for me. Hathaya!

368
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:05,160
Hathaya.

369
00:24:05,240 --> 00:24:08,080
Hathaya. Wait.

370
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:09,920
Please stay and talk to me.

371
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:12,280
I have nothing to talk to you about.

372
00:24:12,360 --> 00:24:15,040
And I don’t think it’s appropriate
for us to talk anymore.

373
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:17,680
I’m your younger brother’s wife.

374
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:22,760
But I’ve been thinking about it.
What happened that night

375
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:24,920
wasn’t true, was it?

376
00:24:25,840 --> 00:24:28,120
Whether it was true or not,
why do you care?

377
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:31,600
You never once asked me
what really happened.

378
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:34,280
Or did you only want to date me

379
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:37,960
because I was useful
for your political interests?

380
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:44,400
That’s not true.

381
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:46,560
You’ve misunderstood me.

382
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:50,240
Forget it. I don’t want
to talk about this anymore.

383
00:24:50,960 --> 00:24:53,160
I don’t want trouble with Chayanee.

384
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:56,080
This has nothing to do with Chayanee.

385
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:58,000
How can it not?

386
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:00,240
I know you and Chayanee are together.

387
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:03,000
Let go of me.

388
00:25:16,280 --> 00:25:17,400
Hathaya!

389
00:25:18,360 --> 00:25:19,680
Are you okay?

390
00:25:20,360 --> 00:25:22,360
I was busy chatting
and wasn’t watching the road.

391
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:24,120
Good thing I braked in time.

392
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:26,600
I’m fine. I should go.

393
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:33,240
You need to drive more carefully.

394
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:36,040
What a shame.

395
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:38,840
What do you mean?

396
00:25:41,520 --> 00:25:42,720
Are you going inside?

397
00:25:47,760 --> 00:25:50,640
I haven’t seen my sister in days.

398
00:25:51,760 --> 00:25:54,640
I thought I’d go say hello.
I’ve missed her so much.

399
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:16,240
This place is actually livable.

400
00:26:16,760 --> 00:26:18,320
I thought it would be a rat hole.

401
00:26:19,640 --> 00:26:21,720
Is there something else
you want from me, Chaya?

402
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:28,560
Why are you talking to me
like we’re strangers?

403
00:26:29,520 --> 00:26:32,160
Ever since you moved into this house,

404
00:26:32,240 --> 00:26:34,360
I’ve missed you so much.

405
00:26:39,560 --> 00:26:41,400
Back when you were in school,

406
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:44,880
you were really good at acting.

407
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:46,880
Everyone always praised you.

408
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:50,520
But I think you’ve gotten
much better at it

409
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:52,080
as an adult.

410
00:26:58,520 --> 00:27:00,360
If you have something to say, just say it.

411
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:11,280
Ever since you moved in with that
crude, low-class husband of yours,

412
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:14,560
you’ve become a lot more vulgar yourself.

413
00:27:17,120 --> 00:27:19,520
I certainly didn’t want
to set foot in this shabby house

414
00:27:19,600 --> 00:27:22,240
belonging to a man I already threw away.

415
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:26,920
Don’t look so shocked.

416
00:27:27,520 --> 00:27:29,200
Your husband

417
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:31,440
is the man I threw away.

418
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:34,480
Back in college,

419
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:36,040
he was crazy about me.

420
00:27:36,120 --> 00:27:38,800
He kept chasing after me,
but I wasn’t interested.

421
00:27:40,040 --> 00:27:42,440
Haven’t you ever noticed?

422
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:46,040
Every time he sees me,
he gets that sour look on his face.

423
00:27:48,160 --> 00:27:50,760
Men are all the same.

424
00:27:50,840 --> 00:27:52,760
Not getting their way wounds their pride.

425
00:27:53,280 --> 00:27:54,960
Then they make things up about me.

426
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:58,760
You don’t have to tell me.
I never wanted to know.

427
00:27:58,840 --> 00:28:00,880
I have to tell you.

428
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:03,120
Otherwise people might gossip

429
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:06,320
that the two of us shared the same man.

430
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:08,200
That would be damaging to my reputation.

431
00:28:09,760 --> 00:28:11,720
You’re worried about your reputation?

432
00:28:12,240 --> 00:28:14,080
But you weren’t embarrassed

433
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:17,400
to date Raiwin after he pursued me?

434
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:18,880
I don’t care.

435
00:28:19,840 --> 00:28:22,120
He was only following his father’s orders

436
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:24,400
and using your good-girl popularity.

437
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:28,560
But now your reputation

438
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:30,640
has been dragged through the mud anyway.

439
00:28:34,360 --> 00:28:35,600
What are you two talking about?

440
00:28:36,640 --> 00:28:37,880
Sounds fun.

441
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:41,680
I’m done talking to my sister.

442
00:28:43,120 --> 00:28:45,400
Have a baby soon, Hathaya.

443
00:28:45,480 --> 00:28:46,880
I’d love to hold my nibling.

444
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:03,080
Why was Chayanee here?

445
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:05,040
Oh.

446
00:29:05,120 --> 00:29:08,680
She came to see Raiwin,
so she stopped by to say hello.

447
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:13,760
Are you hungry? I’m making dinner.
It’s not finished yet.

448
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:15,720
Where’s Max?

449
00:29:16,360 --> 00:29:18,880
He’s sleeping at a friend’s house tonight.

450
00:29:33,080 --> 00:29:34,360
Wait.

451
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:37,240
I don’t want you going to Ramil’s house.

452
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:38,840
Are you jealous?

453
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:42,160
With a girl this pretty,
anyone'd be jealous.

454
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:47,120
Then don’t upset me.

455
00:29:47,880 --> 00:29:48,800
Okay.

456
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:54,240
Want to go eat?

457
00:29:54,320 --> 00:29:55,680
No.

458
00:29:55,760 --> 00:29:58,720
I changed my mind. I want to eat, drink,

459
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:01,360
and spend the night at my condo.

460
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:06,080
Sure. Come on. I’ll drive.

461
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:08,720
Let's go.

462
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:22,120
When he was in college,

463
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:24,240
he raped a woman.

464
00:30:24,320 --> 00:30:27,240
Everything came out
because she got pregnant.

465
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:31,080
Is something wrong?

466
00:30:33,280 --> 00:30:34,960
No. Nothing.

467
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:40,440
What did Chayanee come talk to you about?

468
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:47,080
I told you already.
She just stopped by to say hello.

469
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:49,120
Did she say anything about me?

470
00:30:50,280 --> 00:30:52,680
What do you think

471
00:30:53,200 --> 00:30:54,800
she said about you?

472
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:57,280
I asked you first. Answer me.

473
00:30:58,400 --> 00:31:02,200
I want to know
what you think she said about you.

474
00:31:04,040 --> 00:31:05,200
You…

475
00:31:06,440 --> 00:31:07,440
Forget it.

476
00:31:07,960 --> 00:31:09,960
I don’t want to waste my time
talking about her.

477
00:31:10,040 --> 00:31:12,520
If there’s anything
you’re wondering about me,

478
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:14,200
just ask me directly. Okay?

479
00:31:16,560 --> 00:31:18,400
Go ahead. Anything you want to ask?

480
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:21,200
-No.
-You sure?

481
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:28,040
-Here. Have some egg.
-No, thank you.

482
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:51,360
You’re watching a horror movie?
Perfect atmosphere. It’s raining too.

483
00:31:55,640 --> 00:31:56,480
Turn it up.

484
00:32:04,360 --> 00:32:06,840
What? I’m grabbing the remote.

485
00:32:08,120 --> 00:32:10,800
I told you to turn it up and you didn’t.
Are you deaf?

486
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:18,640
I…

487
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:21,000
I think I’ll just go to bed. I’m sleepy.

488
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:30,680
What? What’s wrong?

489
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:33,760
The thunder startled me.

490
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:41,360
-You’re not watching anymore?
-I’m going to bed.

491
00:32:44,040 --> 00:32:46,160
You put it on and now
you’re not even watching?

492
00:32:56,400 --> 00:33:00,120
Ramil may be aggressive
and rude sometimes,

493
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:03,680
but he doesn’t seem
cruel enough to rape a woman.

494
00:33:10,880 --> 00:33:12,920
-What?
-How did you get in here?

495
00:33:13,760 --> 00:33:14,960
I came to get my earbuds.

496
00:33:17,200 --> 00:33:20,760
Why didn’t you knock first? You scared me.

497
00:33:20,840 --> 00:33:23,760
Stop making a big deal
out of everything. This is my room.

498
00:33:23,840 --> 00:33:25,280
I can come and go whenever I want.

499
00:33:28,920 --> 00:33:30,280
I changed my mind.

500
00:33:31,440 --> 00:33:32,880
I think

501
00:33:34,520 --> 00:33:35,520
I’ll sleep here tonight.

502
00:33:36,480 --> 00:33:38,000
Hey! Don’t.

503
00:33:38,080 --> 00:33:39,320
Why? It’s my bed.

504
00:33:39,920 --> 00:33:41,880
I’m sleeping here. Get out.

505
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:44,840
Get out! I’m sleeping alone.

506
00:33:44,920 --> 00:33:47,160
-No!
-I never should’ve let you stay here.

507
00:33:47,240 --> 00:33:48,480
It’s my room.

508
00:33:49,120 --> 00:33:50,480
You’re so annoying.

509
00:34:05,200 --> 00:34:06,440
Hey, Ramil.

510
00:34:08,920 --> 00:34:11,199
You and I are both
supervisors now. Same level.

511
00:34:12,600 --> 00:34:15,239
We’re not friends.
Don’t act familiar with me.

512
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:16,440
What the hell?

513
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:20,520
You think starting here first
makes you better than me?

514
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:21,440
You servant.

515
00:34:21,520 --> 00:34:23,159
Look at you throwing your weight around

516
00:34:23,239 --> 00:34:26,520
just because Ms. Liu has your back.
You’re just as much of a servant as I am.

517
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:28,120
I came here to talk to you nicely.

518
00:34:28,199 --> 00:34:30,840
I brought my workers over
to introduce them to you.

519
00:34:30,920 --> 00:34:32,080
No need.

520
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:34,520
You and I are working in separate areas.

521
00:34:34,600 --> 00:34:36,040
You do your work, and I’ll do mine.

522
00:34:36,560 --> 00:34:38,920
And I don’t have time for introductions.

523
00:34:39,440 --> 00:34:40,880
I actually have work to do.

524
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:51,000
Boss, that guy looks like trouble.

525
00:34:51,080 --> 00:34:52,360
Want us to handle it?

526
00:34:52,440 --> 00:34:54,639
No. Leave him alone for now.

527
00:34:55,520 --> 00:34:56,719
Let’s get to work.

528
00:34:57,240 --> 00:35:00,000
We’ll show them how much better we are.

529
00:35:00,840 --> 00:35:02,200
Come on. Let’s go.

530
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:17,080
I don’t trust Pong and his people.
They act like thugs.

531
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:20,800
Me neither. I’d love to punch him.

532
00:35:20,880 --> 00:35:22,280
Then why didn’t you?

533
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:26,040
Come on. He works for Ms. Liu.

534
00:35:27,840 --> 00:35:31,080
Forget about him.
We’ll each do our own work.

535
00:35:31,160 --> 00:35:33,000
The results will speak for themselves.

536
00:35:33,840 --> 00:35:36,280
Please help look after our workers.

537
00:35:36,920 --> 00:35:39,720
I’m worried Pong
and his people might cause trouble.

538
00:35:41,520 --> 00:35:42,600
Don’t worry.

539
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:45,320
I’ll take great care of our people.

540
00:35:54,240 --> 00:35:55,160
Boss.

541
00:35:57,520 --> 00:35:59,360
That sounded really cool.

542
00:36:00,560 --> 00:36:03,400
But when you say "our people",

543
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:07,040
do you mean our,

544
00:36:08,280 --> 00:36:11,600
our?

545
00:36:12,600 --> 00:36:15,480
Or our people?

546
00:36:20,920 --> 00:36:21,880
You’re disgusting.

547
00:36:23,080 --> 00:36:25,400
I’m kidding.

548
00:36:26,880 --> 00:36:28,880
It’s not what you think, Max.

549
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:33,000
I’m going back to work.

550
00:36:34,880 --> 00:36:36,640
I’m just kidding.

551
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:47,040
Boss, Miss Hathaya

552
00:36:47,880 --> 00:36:49,880
is pretty cute.

553
00:36:50,480 --> 00:36:54,160
Everyone already thinks you two

554
00:36:54,240 --> 00:36:56,040
are husband and wife anyway.

555
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:57,720
Might as well make it real.

556
00:36:58,840 --> 00:37:00,960
You’re still talking?
Go. Get back to work.

557
00:37:01,040 --> 00:37:03,480
Can’t even tease you anymore.

558
00:37:16,240 --> 00:37:18,680
Drive carefully. Let me know
when you get home.

559
00:37:18,760 --> 00:37:20,160
Okay, darling.

560
00:37:22,960 --> 00:37:23,800
Bye.

561
00:37:36,320 --> 00:37:38,480
Where did you spend the night?

562
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:39,880
Why didn’t you answer my call?

563
00:37:42,400 --> 00:37:44,480
You’re about to enter politics.

564
00:37:45,320 --> 00:37:48,240
You can’t spend every day
relaxing and going out.

565
00:37:48,320 --> 00:37:50,600
Candidate registration is coming up.
You know that.

566
00:37:51,560 --> 00:37:53,920
Use the fact that
I’m still Subdistrict Chief

567
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:55,680
and spend time meeting people.

568
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:59,320
Yes. I’m sorry, Dad.

569
00:38:02,600 --> 00:38:03,720
And from now on,

570
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:07,840
you’re going to stop seeing Chayanee.

571
00:38:21,480 --> 00:38:23,040
Raiwin forgot his phone again.

572
00:38:23,560 --> 00:38:26,560
UNKNOWN NUMBER

573
00:38:27,200 --> 00:38:30,480
I don’t understand you, Dad.
Why don’t you like Chayanee?

574
00:38:30,560 --> 00:38:33,280
She comes from a good family,
she’s well educated,

575
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:35,720
and we’ve been together for a long time.

576
00:38:35,800 --> 00:38:37,840
Because Chayanee is spoiled.

577
00:38:37,920 --> 00:38:40,920
She controls everything you do.
For the past few days,

578
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:43,520
hasn’t she been forcing you
to spend all your time with her?

579
00:38:43,600 --> 00:38:45,680
I can manage my time, Dad.

580
00:38:46,200 --> 00:38:48,720
I promise I won’t let it affect my work.

581
00:38:49,440 --> 00:38:51,480
You're far too gullible.

582
00:38:51,560 --> 00:38:53,200
Why do you let a woman lead you around?

583
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:55,040
I’m ordering you now.

584
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:59,520
Stop seeing this woman. You will obey me.

585
00:38:59,600 --> 00:39:00,440
Understand?

586
00:39:02,480 --> 00:39:03,600
Yes.

587
00:39:09,120 --> 00:39:10,240
Chayanee.

588
00:39:15,240 --> 00:39:16,120
Hello, Uncle.

589
00:39:20,760 --> 00:39:22,680
I’m sorry for interrupting.

590
00:39:24,640 --> 00:39:26,960
But since I already heard everything,

591
00:39:27,040 --> 00:39:29,400
may I ask you something?

592
00:39:29,960 --> 00:39:32,640
Am I not good enough to be
your daughter-in-law?

593
00:39:35,640 --> 00:39:37,560
I don’t dislike you at all, Chayanee.

594
00:39:38,080 --> 00:39:40,440
But right now, I need Raiwin

595
00:39:40,520 --> 00:39:42,280
to focus on preparing for the election.

596
00:39:42,360 --> 00:39:44,400
But we don’t have to break up.

597
00:39:46,520 --> 00:39:48,280
I’ll be straightforward.

598
00:39:49,160 --> 00:39:52,320
I don't want Raiwin to date right now.
It takes up too much time.

599
00:39:52,400 --> 00:39:54,480
I need him to spend all his time

600
00:39:54,560 --> 00:39:57,080
going out into the community

601
00:39:57,160 --> 00:39:58,560
and campaigning.

602
00:39:59,080 --> 00:40:00,560
-Do you understand?
-No!

603
00:40:02,920 --> 00:40:03,880
Look.

604
00:40:04,680 --> 00:40:06,760
I’ll talk to Dad myself.

605
00:40:06,840 --> 00:40:09,120
No. You never manage
to accomplish anything.

606
00:40:09,200 --> 00:40:10,920
I’ll handle this myself.

607
00:40:12,080 --> 00:40:13,200
Uncle,

608
00:40:13,800 --> 00:40:16,040
you said you didn’t want
Raiwin to have a girlfriend

609
00:40:16,120 --> 00:40:18,920
because it would waste his time
and you wanted him to focus on work,

610
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:21,120
but you went to Grandpa and begged him

611
00:40:21,200 --> 00:40:23,800
to let Raiwin date Hathaya.

612
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:27,280
That sounds pretty contradictory to me.

613
00:40:28,400 --> 00:40:30,400
If you didn’t want Raiwin
to have a girlfriend,

614
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:32,400
why did you tell him to pursue Hathaya?

615
00:40:32,480 --> 00:40:34,080
Because Hathaya

616
00:40:34,720 --> 00:40:35,760
is better than you.

617
00:40:36,520 --> 00:40:37,800
Better how?

618
00:40:38,360 --> 00:40:40,240
We’re both Grandpa’s granddaughters.

619
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:42,440
And I’m Grandpa’s favorite.

620
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:45,440
My background is even better
than Hathaya’s.

621
00:40:45,520 --> 00:40:47,400
Yes. Your background is better.

622
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:50,920
But when it comes to reputation
and public attention,

623
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:53,560
you can’t compete with her.

624
00:40:57,040 --> 00:40:59,360
I understand.

625
00:40:59,440 --> 00:41:02,120
You wanted Raiwin to ride
Hathaya’s popularity.

626
00:41:03,520 --> 00:41:06,200
But your plan is over now.
It completely fell apart.

627
00:41:06,280 --> 00:41:07,560
Exactly. It fell apart.

628
00:41:07,640 --> 00:41:10,160
That’s why I can’t let
anything else fall apart.

629
00:41:10,240 --> 00:41:12,520
Raiwin has to become
Subdistrict Chief after me.

630
00:41:12,600 --> 00:41:15,200
I need him out in the community
as much as possible!

631
00:41:15,280 --> 00:41:18,600
Winning over voters takes more than time.

632
00:41:19,120 --> 00:41:21,000
It takes money too.

633
00:41:26,080 --> 00:41:29,160
I’ll financially support Raiwin
in this election.

634
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:31,480
What do you think, Uncle?

635
00:41:36,920 --> 00:41:38,120
Dad.

636
00:41:46,680 --> 00:41:47,640
Raiwin,

637
00:41:48,560 --> 00:41:50,560
you really do know how to choose.

638
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:55,520
You picked Chayanee to be
my daughter-in-law.

639
00:41:58,520 --> 00:42:00,360
Thank you so much, Chayanee.

640
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:07,400
Whether Raiwin becomes Subdistrict Chief

641
00:42:08,280 --> 00:42:09,640
may depend on you now.

642
00:42:12,840 --> 00:42:14,600
I think

643
00:42:15,560 --> 00:42:17,680
we may need

644
00:42:19,160 --> 00:42:20,680
around ten million.

645
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:26,960
I won’t disappoint you.

646
00:42:32,360 --> 00:42:33,400
Raiwin.

647
00:42:38,640 --> 00:42:42,000
I don’t want Chayanee driving home alone.

648
00:42:42,080 --> 00:42:43,240
It’s dangerous.

649
00:42:44,480 --> 00:42:46,280
Drive her

650
00:42:46,840 --> 00:42:48,120
all the way home.

651
00:42:50,640 --> 00:42:51,600
Yes.

652
00:42:54,160 --> 00:42:55,160
Let's go.

653
00:43:22,640 --> 00:43:23,480
What are you making?

654
00:43:24,640 --> 00:43:27,240
Seafood tom yum.

655
00:43:27,320 --> 00:43:28,440
Go sit down and wait.

656
00:43:28,520 --> 00:43:29,720
Come on. I’ll help.

657
00:43:29,800 --> 00:43:30,800
No.

658
00:43:32,720 --> 00:43:33,960
I’ll do it myself.

659
00:43:35,080 --> 00:43:36,000
It’s okay.

660
00:43:38,320 --> 00:43:40,600
Listen, I don’t like to brag,

661
00:43:40,680 --> 00:43:42,640
but when it comes to tom yum,
I’m number one.

662
00:43:42,720 --> 00:43:45,560
If I didn’t have to work for Mr. Pichai,

663
00:43:45,640 --> 00:43:47,080
I'd be on MasterChef Thailand.

664
00:43:48,280 --> 00:43:49,800
-Not that I like to brag.
-Hey!

665
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:55,240
Really, it’s fine. Go sit down.

666
00:43:55,320 --> 00:43:57,160
I’ll call you when it’s ready.

667
00:44:02,480 --> 00:44:03,520
Yeah.

668
00:44:12,800 --> 00:44:16,760
You’re good at this, right?
Then I’ll let you season it.

669
00:44:17,640 --> 00:44:18,840
I’m going to…

670
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:21,880
Where are you going?

671
00:44:25,320 --> 00:44:28,440
I just remembered
I left the air conditioner on.

672
00:44:28,520 --> 00:44:31,880
I’m going to turn it off.
Save you some electricity.

673
00:44:36,640 --> 00:44:38,320
Could you let me through?

674
00:44:40,320 --> 00:44:41,600
Okay.

675
00:44:51,760 --> 00:44:54,200
He can’t be trusted.
I need to keep my distance.

676
00:44:57,360 --> 00:44:59,120
I thought you came to turn off the AC.

677
00:44:59,920 --> 00:45:01,320
What are you doing out here?

678
00:45:02,240 --> 00:45:05,200
I already turned it off.
I just turned it off a second ago.

679
00:45:08,400 --> 00:45:09,600
Hey!

680
00:45:12,880 --> 00:45:14,080
The AC wasn’t even on.

681
00:45:15,600 --> 00:45:18,440
I told you. I just turned it off.

682
00:45:18,520 --> 00:45:19,440
Hey.

683
00:45:22,040 --> 00:45:23,680
Do you think I’m that stupid?

684
00:45:24,280 --> 00:45:27,080
You think I can’t tell
whether a room is cold?

685
00:45:27,760 --> 00:45:28,840
What’s really going on?

686
00:45:32,240 --> 00:45:33,240
I've noticed for a while.

687
00:45:35,800 --> 00:45:36,920
Why are you avoiding me?

688
00:45:39,680 --> 00:45:42,240
Answer me. Why are you avoiding me?

689
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:47,440
Well? Tell me.

690
00:45:47,520 --> 00:45:49,080
Because I’m scared of you.

691
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:51,680
You raped a woman and got her pregnant.

692
00:45:54,800 --> 00:45:55,920
Is it true?

693
00:46:01,440 --> 00:46:04,680
Hey. Wait.

694
00:46:05,320 --> 00:46:07,400
Hey! Don’t run away from the problem.

695
00:46:07,480 --> 00:46:08,960
Talk to me so we can clear this up.

696
00:46:09,040 --> 00:46:10,200
Hey.

697
00:46:10,280 --> 00:46:13,480
I’m not running away.
I just can’t be bothered to answer.

698
00:46:13,560 --> 00:46:16,960
You have to answer.
You’re the one who told me that

699
00:46:17,040 --> 00:46:19,000
if I had questions,
I should ask you directly.

700
00:46:19,080 --> 00:46:20,920
Well, I’m asking you directly now.

701
00:46:22,920 --> 00:46:24,640
If I were really who she says I am,

702
00:46:27,920 --> 00:46:29,680
would you be here without me touching you?

703
00:46:31,520 --> 00:46:33,600
Well, if…

704
00:46:33,680 --> 00:46:36,000
if you didn’t do it, then why

705
00:46:36,520 --> 00:46:38,160
are people still saying you did?

706
00:46:39,400 --> 00:46:40,520
Who is "people"?

707
00:46:46,600 --> 00:46:47,560
Chayanee, right?

708
00:46:49,120 --> 00:46:50,240
Look.

709
00:46:50,320 --> 00:46:53,080
Your sister is practically psychotic.

710
00:46:53,160 --> 00:46:54,360
She never stops lying about me.

711
00:46:56,520 --> 00:46:59,080
I understand that you were hurt

712
00:46:59,160 --> 00:47:00,640
when Chayanee rejected you,

713
00:47:01,960 --> 00:47:04,640
but that doesn’t mean you should
make up things about a woman.

714
00:47:04,720 --> 00:47:08,120
Wait. What? Who rejected who?

715
00:47:09,880 --> 00:47:13,600
You liked Chayanee back in college.
You kept pursuing her.

716
00:47:13,680 --> 00:47:15,520
But when she wasn’t interested,

717
00:47:16,040 --> 00:47:18,920
you started doing all this.

718
00:47:22,040 --> 00:47:24,880
Aren't you a naive little angel?

719
00:47:26,120 --> 00:47:27,000
Listen,

720
00:47:28,440 --> 00:47:31,080
I’m the one who rejected Chayanee.

721
00:47:31,160 --> 00:47:32,200
What?!

722
00:47:33,640 --> 00:47:36,000
-You rejected Chayanee?
-Yes.

723
00:47:37,120 --> 00:47:39,640
I may look rough and crude,

724
00:47:40,600 --> 00:47:41,520
but I’m hot stuff.

725
00:47:42,920 --> 00:47:44,240
Chayanee pursued me.

726
00:47:44,960 --> 00:47:48,080
I wasn’t interested. And I couldn’t
stand her either. You know why?

727
00:47:48,160 --> 00:47:49,720
Because she’s spoiled.

728
00:47:50,240 --> 00:47:52,800
And when Chayanee was pursuing me,

729
00:47:52,880 --> 00:47:54,160
she was also pursuing Raiwin.

730
00:47:54,960 --> 00:47:58,480
I don’t like people who play around. Okay?

731
00:47:59,640 --> 00:48:02,480
Anything else you want to know?
Anything else to clear up?

732
00:48:06,040 --> 00:48:10,000
If you didn’t do it, why don’t you
clear your name?

733
00:48:10,920 --> 00:48:13,080
Everyone has the wrong idea about you.

734
00:48:14,440 --> 00:48:16,560
I don’t care what anyone thinks.

735
00:48:17,880 --> 00:48:20,960
I only tell the truth
to people I really care about.

736
00:48:47,640 --> 00:48:50,040
The tom yum is boiling.

737
00:48:50,920 --> 00:48:53,680
Go check it. You’re the one seasoning it,
aren’t you? Go.

738
00:48:54,360 --> 00:48:56,120
Before it burns. Go.

739
00:49:09,040 --> 00:49:10,440
Are you a friend of Ramil’s?

740
00:49:10,520 --> 00:49:11,640
Mom isn’t his friend.

741
00:49:12,240 --> 00:49:13,200
Daddy!

742
00:49:13,280 --> 00:49:16,120
Why did you lie to me
about having a wife and child?

743
00:49:16,200 --> 00:49:18,680
Hey. Hey!

744
00:49:18,760 --> 00:49:22,320
You can’t buy love with money.

745
00:49:22,400 --> 00:49:25,240
I’m going to use this money
to show Grandpa

746
00:49:25,320 --> 00:49:26,960
that I made the right decision.

747
00:49:27,040 --> 00:49:29,080
‎NEXT EPISODE

748
00:49:29,160 --> 00:49:31,000
Is there anything
you would like me to do, sir?

749
00:51:30,040 --> 00:51:33,880
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
